@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Planning authority and application discovery
+
+The national Planning Data API does not currently contain planning applications for every English local planning authority. ThemePark Map therefore performs a second, bounded discovery stage when England open data or planning documents are enabled.
+
+## Discovery sequence
+
+1. Query Planning Data at the park centre for the responsible `local-planning-authority` boundary.
+2. Match that authority against the built-in or user-supplied portal registry.
+3. Open only the configured authority search form and configured listing pages.
+4. Search a bounded list of park, address and postcode aliases.
+5. Follow only Public Access application-detail links returned by those searches.
+6. Extract application metadata and direct plan/document attachment links.
+7. Feed the resulting applications into the planning-document catalogue.
+
+The first verified built-in portal is Staffordshire Moorlands District Council, including Alton Towers aliases. Additional authorities can be supplied through `--planning-portal-config` without modifying the compiler.
+
+## Geometry safety
+
+Portal search results usually provide an application address and documents but not a reusable georeferenced site polygon. Portal application features are therefore marked:
+
+- `render_in_world: false`
+- `merge_policy: semantic-only`
+- `planning_geometry_role: site-boundary-unlocated`
+- `geometry_is_approximate: true`
+
+They cannot replace OSM. A site, landscape, path or ride plan must first be vectorised and georeferenced, then pass the existing planning-authority status, confidence, overlap, offset and ambiguity gates.
+
+## Portal registry
+
+```json
+{
+  "portals": [
+    {
+      "id": "example-public-access",
+      "type": "idox-public-access",
+      "authorityName": "Example District Council",
+      "lpaReferences": ["E60000000"],
+      "searchUrl": "https://planning.example.gov.uk/portal/servlets/ApplicationSearchServlet",
+      "listingUrls": [],
+      "siteAliasMatch": "example park",
+      "siteAliases": ["Example Park", "Park Lane", "AB1 2CD"]
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## Evidence output
+
+`planning-authority-discovery.json` records the resolved authority, portal, aliases, queries, application links, relevant applications, attachment counts, cache use and warnings. A zero-application result is now explicit as one of:
+
+- `authority-not-found`
+- `portal-not-configured`
+- `no-site-aliases`
+- `no-application-links`
+- `no-relevant-applications`
+diff -ruN v012_authority_discovery_base/src/cli.mjs v012_authority_discovery_work/src/cli.mjs
